          "post_id": "531285",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following two graphs $G$ (on left), $H$(on right):</p><p style=\"text-align:center\"><img alt=\"\" width=\"550\" height=\"258\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p><br>Which of the following statements is/are true for $G$, $H$ ?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>The above two graphs have the same number of vertices.<br> </li><li>The above two graphs have the same number of edges.<br> </li><li>The above two graphs have the same degree sequences.<br> </li><li>The above two graphs are isomorphic.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;b;c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses_cs_wq66,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,graph-theory,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Graph Theory"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "531289",
          "text": "What is the maximum number of vertices on a graph that has $35$ edges and every vertex has degree $\\geq 3$ ?",
