          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements is/are true?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>If two graphs have the same number of vertices and the same number of cycles of each order, then they are isomorphic.</li><li>Two isomorphic graphs must have the same number of edges and vertices.</li><li>Two isomorphic graphs always look exactly the same.</li><li>Isomorphism is an equivalence relation on all graphs.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "b;d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses_cs_wq66,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,graph-theory,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Graph Theory"
        },
