          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "531283",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following graphs cannot exist ? (Select all that apply)</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>A graph with an isolated vertex and a universal vertex. (Note: A universal vertex is a vertex of an undirected graph that is adjacent to all other vertices of the graph.)<br> </li><li>A cubic graph of order 5. (Note: A cubic graph is a graph in which all vertices have degree three.)<br> </li><li>A bipartite graph of order 5 and size 7.<br> </li><li>A bipartite graph of order 8 and size 10.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;b;c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses_cs_wq66,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,graph-theory,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Graph Theory"
        },
